WEBVTT

00:00:00.232 --> 00:00:04.549
Welcome to VPSHR Level Zero the Voluntary Principles on

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.672
Security and Human Rights This course introduces the

00:00:08.737 --> 00:00:11.662
connection between responsible security and respect for

00:00:11.726 --> 00:00:15.528
people's rights It gives us a shared foundation for

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:17.319
the decisions we make at work

00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:22.335
You will explore human rights the responsibilities of

00:00:22.348 --> 00:00:25.763
employees and security personnel and situations that

00:00:25.802 --> 00:00:29.358
can put people at risk As you learn think

00:00:29.358 --> 00:00:34.113
about your own workplace Who could be affected What

00:00:34.204 --> 00:00:37.838
could go wrong What would a responsible response look

00:00:37.889 --> 00:00:38.198
like

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.401
Start with the learning unit shown on your course

00:00:42.465 --> 00:00:46.873
page Within a presentation use the slide arrows to

00:00:46.886 --> 00:00:51.241
move between slides Use the platform's next unit button

00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:53.162
only when you are ready to leave the whole

00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:57.762
learning unit This introduction is a single video so

00:00:57.762 --> 00:00:59.605
it has no separate next button

00:01:01.273 --> 00:01:04.611
You control the pace Pause when you need time

00:01:04.688 --> 00:01:08.515
to think replay an explanation and turn on captions

00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:12.381
using the video controls You can also enlarge the

00:01:12.446 --> 00:01:15.358
presentation or use full screen where those controls

00:01:15.423 --> 00:01:18.889
are available You can return to an earlier unit

00:01:18.902 --> 00:01:20.448
to revisit its content

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.099
Work through the activities and quizzes included in

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:28.668
each learning unit Read the instructions before

00:01:28.681 --> 00:01:32.071
answering and check any stated pass mark or attempt

00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:36.053
limit Use feedback to improve your understanding

00:01:36.994 --> 00:01:40.344
Watching a video or seeing a completion tick does

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.664
not by itself demonstrate competence

00:01:44.357 --> 00:01:47.436
If you need help use Messages and support on

00:01:47.514 --> 00:01:51.122
the platform Tell us the course name the learning

00:01:51.174 --> 00:01:53.880
unit and the slide or activity where you got

00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:57.501
stuck Describe what happened so that we can help

00:01:57.565 --> 00:01:58.248
you continue

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.316
Take your time ask questions and connect what you

00:02:03.342 --> 00:02:05.971
learn to the way people are treated in practice

00:02:06.886 --> 00:02:09.566
We wish you a valuable and rewarding learning journey

00:02:10.468 --> 00:02:13.677
When this video finishes stay on this page until

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.143
you are ready Then use the platform's next unit

00:02:17.233 --> 00:02:18.200
button to begin
